For the first time, a broad smile cracks her face. "A savior. Truly, the opener of the ways who can rescue marooned travelers." She turns and speaks to her crewmates. "Challan askun toveld! Getsa!"

She turns back to you and presses a small device into your hand. "Is useful. Old but reliable."

{LOOT}

candidates.translation:
她脸上第一次绽开灿烂的笑容。“救世主。当真是开路者，能救回迷途旅人。”她转身对同伴们说了什么。“Challan askun toveld! Getsa!”

她转回身，将一个小装置塞进你手中。“有用。旧了，但可靠。”

{LOOT}

candidates.source:
[Look more closely at the eggs that have gone out entirely.]

{NATHAN: My idea here is that if the player has one of these skill options (currenty Lore: Natural Science, Lore: Wilderness, or Visual Perception), they will pick up on the fact that the unnamed eggs are giving energy to the named ones. They can go back and tell Cintra what they saw along with their good interpretation: that Cintra's child is enabling the other ghibra children to live and grow stronger, thus making the community stronger as a whole.

(Or better: give the player multiple interpretations to what they saw, each based on different Tides, allowing them to comfort Cintra or not.)}

